<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  DARK-MODE LAUNCH (admin 2026-08-13: "native app lage, capacitor nahi").

  These styles cover the moment BEFORE the WebView paints. The app's own UI already follows the
  user's theme, and the splash is already dark (capacitor.config.ts, backgroundColor #0d1117) — but
  the Activity window underneath had no dark variant, so a phone in dark mode could flash a light
  window between the splash handing off and React painting. It is a fraction of a second, and it is
  exactly the fraction that reads as "a web page is loading".

  Only the WINDOW background is overridden. The splash drawable is unchanged, because it is already
  drawn on the app's own dark surface in both themes.
-->
<resources>
    <style name="AppTheme" parent="Theme.AppCompat.DayNight.DarkActionBar">
        <item name="colorPrimary">@color/colorPrimary</item>
        <item name="colorPrimaryDark">@color/colorPrimaryDark</item>
        <item name="colorAccent">@color/colorAccent</item>
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@color/nbaiSurfaceDark</item>
    </style>

    <style name="AppTheme.NoActionBar" parent="Theme.AppCompat.DayNight.NoActionBar">
        <item name="windowActionBar">false</item>
        <item name="windowNoTitle">true</item>
        <item name="android:background">@null</item>
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@color/nbaiSurfaceDark</item>
    </style>

    <!--
      `AppTheme.NoActionBarLaunch` IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT, and this is the subtle part.

      Android resolves a resource by eliminating candidate folders qualifier by qualifier, and NIGHT
      MODE ranks ABOVE API VERSION in that order. So on an Android 12+ phone in dark mode, a copy of
      this style here would match the night qualifier, eliminate values-v31/ outright, and take away
      the `windowSplashScreenBackground` that folder exists to set — leaving the system splash white
      in dark mode, which is the one place the flash is most obvious.

      Leaving it undeclared keeps this style's candidates at values/ and values-v31/, neither of
      which mentions night, so the version qualifier decides and v31 wins in BOTH themes. Nothing is
      lost by omitting it: the launch theme draws @drawable/splash, which is already the app's own
      dark surface regardless of theme.
    -->
</resources>
